course: dictionary
lesson: 15813
title: Uncleanliness and dirt
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Uncleanliness means being dirty or not clean. The ending -liness turns the describing word unclean into a naming word, something you can point to. «The inspector found uncleanliness in the kitchen: dirty pans and crumbs on the floor.» The clues dirty pans and crumbs tell you the kitchen was not clean.
explain: Uncleanliness can also be a habit, the way you keep yourself and your things. «Sam never cleaned his room, and his mum said the uncleanliness had to stop.» Sam's room is dirty because he does not clean it, so uncleanliness here means that habit of not keeping things clean.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. Try «the dirtiness had to stop» or «the not being clean had to stop». Both still make sense, so dirtiness is the right idea. If a meaning does not fit the sentence, try another one.
fact: Uncleanliness means the state of being dirty or not clean.
fact: Uncleanliness can also mean the habit of not keeping yourself or your things clean.
fact: In older Bible translations, uncleanliness can mean not pure in God's eyes or by religious rules.
fact: Dirt can carry germs, so uncleanliness in kitchens and hospitals can make people ill.
fact: Uncleanliness is an uncountable noun: you say «a lot of uncleanliness», not «an uncleanliness».
exercise: «The inspector found uncleanliness in the kitchen.» What does uncleanliness mean here? | *Dirt and not being clean | A cold, quiet room | Shiny new equipment | Kind words from the cook
exercise: «Ali washed his hands and cleaned his desk every day, so he had no uncleanliness.» What does this tell you? | He was very dirty | He was too tired to play | *He kept himself and his things clean | He ate too much food
exercise: «Uncleanliness can make people ill.» Which sentence means the same? | *Being dirty can make people ill | Being clean always helps people sleep | Being hungry makes people cross | Being happy can make people ill
test: «A girl who never cleans her room each week shows what?» | A clean kitchen | A shiny bike | *Uncleanliness as a habit | Good manners
test: In older Bible translations, what can uncleanliness mean? | Eating too fast | *Not pure by God's or religious rules | Being very tall | Having a loud voice
exam: Which sentence uses uncleanliness correctly? | We went uncleanliness to the park | The cat has uncleanliness | He is very uncleanliness today | *The kitchen was full of uncleanliness, with dirty pans and crumbs
